    Convert a numeral that nothing fixes into its default in the compiled checker, and refuse one out of range

    Under the one type `IntLiteral` the team's checker kept a numeral's own type wherever nothing converted it, so `bigN = 3000000000` read as a `ZZ32` at a tie and died when it ran ('java.lang.Error: Not in range for ZZ32: 3000000000'), `a: ZZ32 = 4294967295` compiled and raised at run time, and `7` at a parameter of type `Object` took no `ZZ32` clause where the interpreter took it. The checker now converts such a numeral into `ZZ32`, `ZZ64` or `ZZ` by its value or `RR64` with a radix point, refuses a numeral out of range statically, writes the numeral types only as a parameter's type, and reads a size used as a value as a `ZZ32` (climb batch 29, rung C; P-173, P-174, P-40). The gather corrects Appendix I's `revival-index` sentence on a numeral at `Index`.

